The standard deviation of the sampling distribution of the sample mean (i.e., the standard error under the null hypothesis) is  

\[
\sigma_{\bar{x}}=\frac{s}{\sqrt{n}}
=\frac{1.4}{\sqrt{40}}
\approx \frac{1.4}{6.3249}
\approx 0.221\; .
\]

So the null‑hypothesis test’s standard deviation (standard error) is **≈ 0.22**.
